      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match report",
          "heading": "Ireland women seal seven-try victory over Japan in Cork test",
          "body": "The Ireland women’s side secured a comprehensive 43-19 win against Japan at Virgin Media Park on Saturday. After an early deficit, Scott Bemand’s team responded with four first-half tries before pulling away after the interval. Beibhinn Parsons extended her all-time international try-scoring record to 25, while Alana McInerney and Sophie Barrett marked their respective debuts with second-half scores. The victory follows a win against the same opponents in Galway last week, providing momentum ahead of the upcoming WXV series."
        },
